.TH spin 1 "Dec 2024" "" "General Commands Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.
.SH NAME
spin \- Command-line spinner tool for long-running processes
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spin
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ ARG ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBspin\fP is a command-line tool written in C++ that displays an animated spinner while a background process is running. It is useful for visually indicating that a task is in progress, especially if the task takes a considerable amount of time.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.
.SS General options:
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display this help message and exit
.TP
.B --version
Show program's version number and exit
.TP
.B -t TEXT, --text=TEXT
Text to show alongside the spinner
.TP
.B -i INT, --interval=INT
Interval in milliseconds between spinner updates
.TP
.B --style=NAME
Style/name of the spinner to use
.TP
.B --cmd=COMMAND
Command to execute while displaying the spinner
.TP
.B -c COLOR, --color=COLOR
Change text color (use number)
.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Run quietly, suppressing output
.
.SS Information options:
.TP
.B --show_colors
Show list of available colors and exit
.TP
.B --show_style
Show list of available spinner styles/symbols and exit
.
.SS Text/Message options:
.TP
.B --result
Display message after execution finishes
.TP
.B -e TEXT, --error=TEXT
Custom error message to display on failure
.TP
.B -s TEXT, --success=TEXT
Custom success message to display on completion
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic usage with custom text:
.B spin -t "Loading.." --cmd "sleep 2"
.TP
With color and interval:
.B spin -t "Processing" -c 105 -i 100 --cmd "long_running_task"
.TP
With success/error messages:
.B spin --cmd "build.sh" -s "Build successful!" -e "Build failed!"
.TP
List available styles:
.B spin --show_style
.TP
Run quietly:
.B spin -q --cmd "backup.sh"
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR https://victorh028.github.io/spin/
.
